      "answer": "According to Cargo's official documentation (The Cargo Book, \"Cargo.toml vs Cargo.lock\"), Cargo.lock is used to record the exact versions of a project's dependencies. The documentation states verbatim: \"Cargo.lock contains exact information about your dependencies. It is maintained by Cargo and should not be manually edited.\" While Cargo.toml describes the abstract dependencies of a project, Cargo.lock pins the concrete versions actually used, ensuring reproducible builds.\n\nSource: https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html\n\nFINAL LABEL: supported",
